<BaseLayout
  title="About Us | MegaMoneyMomentum (MMM)"
  description="Mission, editorial principles, fact-checking standards, and data research methodology of MegaMoneyMomentum (MMM)."
>
  <article class="article-container">
    <header class="article-header">
      <div class="article-category-badge" style="background-color: var(--primary-light); color: var(--primary);">
        About MegaMoneyMomentum
      </div>
      <h1 class="article-title">Guiding Financial & Tax Decisions in South Korea with Transparency</h1>
      <div class="article-meta">
        <span>Published by MegaMoneyMomentum Global Editorial Team</span>
        <span>•</span>
        <span>Updated: 2026 Edition</span>
      </div>
    </header>

    <div class="article-content">
      <p>
        <strong>MegaMoneyMomentum (MMM)</strong> is an independent digital financial media platform dedicated to providing transparent, accurate, and actionable financial, tax, and living guides for Korean citizens and foreign residents (expats, digital nomads, and investors) in South Korea.
      </p>

      <div class="callout-box">
        <div class="callout-title">✓ Our 3 Core Editorial & Fact-Checking Principles</div>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Primary Official Sources:</strong> Every article is verified against primary data from the National Tax Service (NTS), Ministry of Economy and Finance (MOEF), Financial Supervisory Service (FSS), and Bank of Korea.</li>
          <li><strong>Zero Financial Conflicts of Interest:</strong> We do not offer unlicensed investment solicitation. All content is strictly educational and analytical.</li>
          <li><strong>Continuous Policy Updates:</strong> With Korea's rapid regulatory and tax amendments, our team updates calculations and eligibility rules in real-time.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <h2>What We Cover</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Tax & Expat Settlement:</strong> Year-end tax settlement, 19% flat tax rate for foreign workers, global income tax, and capital gains exemptions.</li>
        <li><strong>Wealth & Retirement:</strong> Individual Savings Accounts (ISA), Individual Retirement Pensions (IRP), US index ETFs (S&P 500, Dividend ETFs), and compound growth.</li>
        <li><strong>Smart Living & Travel Money:</strong> National Health Insurance (NHIS) refund claims, subway passes (Climate Card, T-Money, WOWPASS), and instant tax refunds at Incheon Airport.</li>
        <li><strong>Credit & Banking:</strong> Credit score optimization (KCB/NICE), non-face-to-face emergency loans, and interest rate reduction requests.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Editorial Inquiries & Contact</h2>
      <p>
        We welcome reader feedback, corrections, and partnership inquiries.
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Email:</strong> contact@megamomo.co.kr</li>
        <li><strong>Website:</strong> https://www.megamomo.co.kr</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
